# Project Layout (production agents & APIs)

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|-------|----------|----------------|
| API | `api/routers/` | HTTP routes, auth, Pydantic schemas — no graph or DB logic |
| Service | `services/` | Invoke graphs/RAG pipelines, map errors, transactions |
| Graph | `graphs/` | LangGraph `StateGraph` — nodes, edges, routing |
| Agent | `agents/` | Single-agent nodes; supervisor via `langgraph-supervisor` |
| Tool | `tools/` | LangChain `@tool` — one external action each |
| RAG | `rag/` or `pipelines/` | Ingestion, chunking, embedding, retrieval |
| Core | `core/` | Settings, LLM factory, DB session, graph compilation |

# RAG Pipelines

- Ingestion: PyMuPDF or equivalent → chunk with overlap → embed via Ollama local → store in ChromaDB.
- Keep retrieval strategy (Naive / HyDE / Reranking) pluggable; never mix embedding and generation backends silently.
- Return source citations with answers to reduce hallucinations.

```python
# ✅ GOOD — strategy injected, traced run
result = await rag_service.query(
    question=body.question,
    strategy=settings.retrieval_strategy,
    trace_id=run_id,
)
```

# LangGraph & Agents

- Graph state: `TypedDict` or Pydantic model — never loose dicts between nodes.
- Nodes are pure: read state → call tool/service → return partial update.
- Tools need explicit names and descriptions (LLM contract).
- Use `graph.ainvoke()` / `astream()` from async handlers; compile at startup.
- Multi-agent: supervisor in `agents/`, workers as subgraphs or dedicated nodes.

# FastAPI & Persistence

- SQLModel models in `models/`; Pydantic DTOs in `schemas/` — never expose ORM models in responses.
- Inject `Session` via `Depends(get_session)`; commit in service layer, not in graph nodes.
- Wrap sync `requests` calls with `asyncio.to_thread` inside async paths; set timeouts.

# Streamlit Prototypes

- UI in `app.py` or `pages/`; call shared service/RAG modules — no duplicated pipeline logic.
- Show latency and source snippets in the interface for manual evaluation.

# Testing & Evaluation

- Unit-test tools and nodes in isolation; integration-test graphs with mocked LLM.
- Benchmark prompting and RAG strategies with RAGAS; log all runs to LangSmith.
